{"assets":["/statement-assets/8018f9382a2ae86cc0cb36d6087d0032035dd6c21a9d6dc88a4b4021ed423ab4.png","/statement-assets/e7e7bafb03040ac239c17d18ffb7a7745064fd27d4c1cd7d2322e71662579b66.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"912","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Fishes"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"While Grisha was celebrating New Year with Ded Moroz, Misha gifted Sasha a small rectangular pond of size "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n × m"},{"kind":"text","text":", divided into cells of size "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 × 1"},{"kind":"text","text":", inhabited by tiny evil fishes (no more than one fish per cell, otherwise they'll strife!)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The gift bundle also includes a square scoop of size "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"r × r"},{"kind":"text","text":", designed for fishing. If the lower-left corner of the scoop-net is located at cell "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(x, y)"},{"kind":"text","text":", all fishes inside the square "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(x, y)...(x + r - 1, y + r - 1)"},{"kind":"text","text":" get caught. Note that the scoop-net should lie completely inside the pond when used."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Unfortunately, Sasha is not that skilled in fishing and hence throws the scoop randomly. In order to not frustrate Sasha, Misha decided to release "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" fishes into the empty pond in such a way that the expected value of the number of caught fishes is as high as possible. Help Misha! In other words, put "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" fishes in the pond into distinct cells in such a way that when the scoop-net is placed into a random position among "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(n - r + 1)·(m - r + 1)"},{"kind":"text","text":" possible positions, the average number of caught fishes is as high as possible."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line contains four integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n, m, r, k"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n, m ≤ 105"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ r ≤ min(n, m)"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ k ≤ min(n·m, 105)"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print a single number — the maximum possible expected number of caught fishes."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You answer is considered correct, is its absolute or relative error does not exceed "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"10 - 9"},{"kind":"text","text":". Namely, let your answer be "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":", and the jury's answer be "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":". Your answer is considered correct, if "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/8018f9382a2ae86cc0cb36d6087d0032035dd6c21a9d6dc88a4b4021ed423ab4.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3 3 2 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2.0000000000\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"12 17 9 40\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"32.8333333333\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example you can put the fishes in cells "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(2, 1)"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(2, 2)"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(2, 3)"},{"kind":"text","text":". In this case, for any of four possible positions of the scoop-net (highlighted with light green), the number of fishes inside is equal to two, and so is the expected value."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/e7e7bafb03040ac239c17d18ffb7a7745064fd27d4c1cd7d2322e71662579b66.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"912D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/912/problem/D"}